{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Hc4hzE33Z3ESUS3V3BbN22","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified by differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system, not to ship utilities.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` for each utility, `pkg/testutils/` for differential testing, `pkg/sys/` for syscall abstractions, `pkg/format/` for output formatting, `pkg/hashutil/`, `pkg/sizeparse/`, `pkg/encutil/` for shared helpers. Specifications live in `docs/specs/`. Code generation is automated; specs are human-authored.\n\n**Current state**: 33 releases defined (00.0 through 15.0), covering 111 utilities. Many utilities are already implemented (code_status shows \"implemented\" for sponge, du, true/false/yes/basename/dirname, tee, head/seq, wc, uname/arch/hostname/hostid, realpath/readlink/pwd/tty, nl/fold, unexpand, paste, uniq/comm, md5sum/sha256sum, mkdir/rmdir/ln/unlink, and others). The requirement_states field shows which SRD sub-requirements remain in \"ready\" status.\n\n**Current release priority**: The earliest release with ready requirements is **rel06.0** (Batch 6.0). Within rel06.0, only **srd036-mktemp** has ready requirements (R3.5, R3.6, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3, R4.4). The other utilities in rel06.0 (mkdir, rmdir, ln, unlink) are already implemented. After rel06.0, the next target is rel06.1 (env, printenv, id, whoami, groups -- all ready).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **rel06.0 srd036-mktemp**: 6 remaining ready requirements (R3.5, R3.6, R4.1-R4.4). Other mktemp requirements (R1.x, R2.x, R3.1-R3.4) are not in \"ready\" status, indicating they were already handled. The package likely exists partially from prior tasks.\n2. **rel06.1**: All five utilities have all requirements ready, but these come after completing rel06.0.\n3. Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks. With 6 requirements and a max of 4 per task, mktemp needs 2 implementation tasks + 2 test tasks = 4 tasks, which fills the task budget.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\nAssuming default weight=1 (requirements.yaml not available in project_context; per spec \"default 1\"):\n\n```\nTask 0: srd036-mktemp R3.5(w=1) + R3.6(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd036-mktemp R4.3(w=1) + R4.4(w=1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd036-mktemp R3.5(w=1) + R3.6(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓ (tests)\nTask 3: srd036-mktemp R4.3(w=1) + R4.4(w=1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓ (tests)\n```\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"srd036-mktemp R3.5, R3.6, R4.1, R4.2 (implementation)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd036-mktemp.yaml (requirements R3.5, R3.6, R4.1, R4.2 -- read these specific requirements and their acceptance criteria)\n      - cmd/mktemp/main.go (existing implementation -- extend without breaking existing functionality)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (SIGPIPE handler convention)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mktemp/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd036-mktemp R3.5, R3.6, R4.1, R4.2\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd036-mktemp requirement R3.5 exactly as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd036-mktemp requirement R3.6 exactly as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd036-mktemp requirement R4.1 exactly as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd036-mktemp requirement R4.2 exactly as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the patterns already established in cmd/mktemp/main.go -- extend the existing flag parsing, template handling, and error reporting rather than restructuring\"\n      - id: D2\n    